        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 29:9",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 29,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "And behold, when I see many of my brethren truly penitent, and coming to the Lord their God, then is my soul filled with joy; then do I remember what the Lord has done for me, yea, even that he hath heard my prayer; yea, then do I remember his merciful arm which he extended towards me.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 145,
            "end": 149,
            "text": "Mosiah 27:14 (11–31)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 29:10",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 29,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Yea, and I also remember the captivity of my fathers; for I surely do know that the Lord did deliver them out of bondage, and by this did establish his church; yea, the Lord God, the God of Abraham, the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob, did deliver them out of bondage.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 88,
            "text": "Ex. 3:6; Alma 36:2."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Ex. 3:6; Alma 36:2.",
            "prettyString": "Exodus 3:6; Alma 36:2",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "exodus",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 3,
                    "end": 3,
                    "verses": [
