        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 29:13",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 29,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "But I do not joy in my own success alone, but my joy is more full because of the success of my brethren, who have been up to the land of Nephi.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 34,
            "text": "Alma 17:4 (1–4)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 29:14",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 29,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, they have labored exceedingly, and have brought forth much fruit; and how great shall be their reward!",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 29:15",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 29,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "Now, when I think of the success of these my brethren my soul is carried away, even to the separation of it from the body, as it were, so great is my joy.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 150,
            "end": 153,
            "text": "TG Joy."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
